From upstream ggml-org/llama.cpp 3e4dfa8f39f9 ("models : add maion-coder", #29778),
the llm_graph_input_k_shift::set_input hunk only. A model with no RoPE layer
(rope_pattern all 0, e.g. Granite-4.0-H: rope.scaling.finetuned=false) builds a
K-shift graph that never reads k_shift, so the input is left without a buffer
and set_input_k_shift aborts on GGML_ASSERT(buffer). Drop at the #522 pin bump
(the pin will contain it; apply-llama-patches.sh then fails on this patch).

diff --git a/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp b/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
index 463510c..b8dc350 100644
--- a/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
@@ -2007,7 +2007,7 @@ public:
 void llm_graph_input_k_shift::set_input(const llama_ubatch * ubatch) {
     GGML_UNUSED(ubatch);
 
-    if (k_shift) {
+    if (k_shift && k_shift->buffer) {
         kv_self->set_input_k_shift(k_shift);
     }
 
